 "case:locations.yard.art.props.9.label": "Lane",
 "case:locations.yard.description": "Hafod’s old farmyard, cobbled and mossy and closed in on three sides: the long stone barn that is now the studio, the farmhouse with its slate porch, and the granary, a squat stone building whose rooms are upstairs, reached by fourteen stone steps up its outside wall. There is no handrail. Bryn’s car is still parked by the farmhouse porch. The police tape has gone; the dark patch on the cobbles hasn’t.",
 "case:locations.yard.hotspots.hs_yd_car.label": "Bryn’s car",
 "case:locations.yard.hotspots.hs_yd_car.text": "Bryn’s old estate car, parked a few metres from the farmhouse porch with its nose to the granary. From the driver’s seat you look straight at the steps, and the farmhouse door sits in the wing mirror.",
 "case:locations.yard.hotspots.hs_yd_farmdoor.label": "The farmhouse door",
 "case:locations.yard.hotspots.hs_yd_farmdoor.text": "A slate porch, a boot rack and a door that sticks. From the porch to the foot of the granary steps is the whole width of the yard: anyone crossing it would be in plain view of the parked cars and the lounge window.",
 "case:locations.yard.hotspots.hs_yd_foot.label": "The foot of the steps",
 "case:locations.yard.hotspots.hs_yd_foot.text": "Where Rhys landed, and where, on the video, Dean shoved him. From here you can see straight across the yard into the big lounge window.",
 "case:locations.yard.hotspots.hs_yd_steps.label": "The granary steps",
 "case:locations.yard.hotspots.hs_yd_steps.text": "Fourteen stone steps climb the granary wall to a landing hardly wider than a doormat. They’re worn hollow in the middle and slick with moss, and the police’s chalk is still on them.",
 "case:locations.yard.hotspots.hs_yd_window.label": "The lounge window",
 "case:locations.yard.hotspots.hs_yd_window.text": "The studio lounge’s big window looks straight across the yard at the granary steps, thirty metres away. At night, with the lamps on inside, you’d see little of the dark yard from that sofa. But when the landing light comes on, it lights the steps like a stage.",
 "case:locations.yard.name": "The Yard",
 "case:locations.yard.summary": "The cobbled farmyard, and the granary steps where Rhys fell.",
 "case:setting": "Hafod · mid-Wales · October 2024",
 "case:sketchCredit": "SKETCH: SITE VISIT, 30 OCTOBER 2024 · NOT TO SCALE",
 "case:sketchTitle": "HAFOD",
 "case:stayLabel": "Stay at Hafod",
 "case:tagline": "A band back together, a song with one name on it, and a fall in the small hours.",
 "case:timeline.conclusion": "The row, Dean’s bedtime and Eddie’s call all happened in the first one o’clock, summer time. Then the clocks went back. Rhys sang the vocal of his life, said goodnight, and climbed the steps in the dark, and at 01:41, the second time round, he fell. By then the only person in the granary was the man whose alibi everyone had already checked.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_ambulance.text": "The ambulance arrives",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_ambulance.time": "02:16",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_clocks.teaser": "Something written in the control room.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_clocks.text": "The clocks go back an hour",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_clocks.time": "02:00 → 01:00",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_dean.teaser": "Something in the farmhouse.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_dean.text": "Dean goes to bed in the farmhouse",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_eddie.teaser": "Something Huw remembers.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_eddie.text": "Eddie says goodnight and goes up to the granary",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_fall.text": "Rhys falls down the granary steps, and his watch calls for help",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_leaves.teaser": "Somebody saw Rhys go.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_leaves.text": "Rhys says goodnight and leaves the studio",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_photo.teaser": "Something posted to the band.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_photo.text": "Bryn posts a photo of Dean asleep",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_ring.teaser": "Something heard after the fall.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_ring.text": "A phone rings beside Rhys’s body",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_row.text": "Dean shoves Rhys at the foot of the granary steps, on Freya’s camera",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_stove.teaser": "Something done on Sunday morning.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_stove.text": "Eddie lights the wood burner in the lounge",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_stove.time": "07:30",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_take6.teaser": "Something the studio computer remembers.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_take6.text": "Take 6: the last take with the whole band",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_take6.time": "00:40",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_take9.teaser": "Something else the studio computer remembers.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_take9.text": "Rhys sings Take 9, his last vocal",
 "case:timeline.prompt": "Put the events in the order they really happened. Times you know for certain are shown; reason out the rest.",
 "case:timeline.title": "Saturday night, reconstructed",
 "case:title": "Silent Partner",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_bryn_bed.insight": "Bryn wasn’t asleep by midnight: he recorded his drums again at 01:38, and posted a photo of Dean asleep to the band chat at 01:12, after the clocks went back. He’d put a very drunk Dean to bed.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_bryn_bed.response.0": "…Right. You’ve got me there.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_bryn_bed.response.1": "I wasn’t in bed by twelve. I did my drums again at gone half one, and then I went over to the farmhouse. Dean was on the stairs — he’d only just come in, and he couldn’t stand. I got him into bed and sat with him. When my phone went back to one I thought, smashing, another hour of this. A bit later I sent the chat that photo.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_bryn_bed.response.2": "Then I went to sleep. Honestly.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_bryn_bed.title": "Bryn was up, with Dean",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_bryn_sleep.insight": "Bryn didn’t sleep after his photo. From quarter past one, second time round, he sat in his car in the yard with a bottle, facing the steps. After the fall he saw someone come down from the top of the steps to Rhys, heard a phone ring, and watched them go back up.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_bryn_sleep.response.0": "…Twelve years. Twelve years and four months.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_bryn_sleep.response.1": "I went out to the car at quarter past one. I keep a bottle in there — I always have, in case. I sat with the window down, facing the granary, and I drank it, and I kept the farmhouse door in my wing mirror in case anyone caught me.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_bryn_sleep.response.2": "I saw Rhys come out of the studio and go up the steps in the dark. Then a thump, and his watch going off, like a little car alarm. I ducked down — I had the bottle in my hand. When I looked again, somebody was coming down the steps from the top with a phone lit up. They bent over him. A phone rang, twice, and then they went back up the steps, fast. A door shut.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_bryn_sleep.response.3": "Nobody came out of that farmhouse until Carys, a few minutes later, screaming. I’ve been too ashamed to say.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_bryn_sleep.title": "Bryn was drinking in his car",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_carys_debt.insight": "In April Eddie’s company lent Carys £60,000, to be repaid out of the sale. If the sale fell through, so would she, and so would Eddie, who had borrowed against it himself.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_carys_debt.response.0": "…My business went under in March. Eddie was kind. He lent me sixty thousand to clear it, out of ‘the Westwater money’, and I never told Rhys.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_carys_debt.response.1": "He said he’d borrowed against the sale himself. Four hundred thousand, on his house. ‘If Monday goes wrong, Carys, we’re both on the street.’",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_carys_debt.response.2": "So yes. I had every reason in the world to want that sale to happen. I didn’t kill my husband for it.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_carys_debt.title": "Carys owed Eddie £60,000",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_carys_row.insight": "On Saturday afternoon Rhys told Carys he was giving Dean half of ‘Small Hours’. They rowed, and she moved out of the granary. If Rhys had lived, she would have lost half of the songs she inherits.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_carys_row.response.0": "…Freya heard that. Of course she did. Half the farm probably heard it.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_carys_row.response.1": "He told me after lunch. He was giving Dean half of ‘Small Hours’, back to the beginning, on Monday. Half our pension, half the house, for a guilty conscience. I said that, and worse. Then I took my bag to the farmhouse.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_carys_row.response.2": "The last real thing I said to my husband was that he was mad.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_carys_row.title": "Carys and Rhys rowed about the song",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_dean_song.insight": "‘Thirty years’ was about ‘Small Hours’. In the yard Rhys told Dean he was putting Dean’s name on the song on Monday, and Dean, drunk, called him a liar and shoved him.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_dean_song.response.0": "…Thirty years. Yeah. It wasn’t about the take.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_dean_song.response.1": "He took me out for that cigarette to tell me. He’d written to PRS. He was putting my name on it, Monday, fifty-fifty, back to the start. He had it all worked out.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_dean_song.response.2": "And I called him a liar. Thirty years, and you think a letter fixes it? I put my hands on him. That’s the last thing I ever said to my best friend.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_dean_song.title": "It was about the song",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_alibi.insight": "Eddie’s call was real, from twenty past one until five to two — in summer time, before the clocks went back. When Rhys fell, at 01:41 the second time round, Eddie had been alone in the granary for three quarters of an hour.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_alibi.response.0": "…So I was on the call at the wrong twenty to two. Is that a crime now, being on a phone call?",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_alibi.response.1": "I said goodnight, I went up, and I went to sleep. I was exhausted. I’m sixty-one.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_alibi.response.2": "But for the first time, he doesn’t hold your eye.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_alibi.title": "Eddie’s call was the first twenty to two",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_bed.insight": "At 18:43 in Los Angeles — 01:43 at Hafod, two minutes after the fall — Westwater’s lawyer rang Eddie, and he declined the call. The 999 line heard his ringtone beside Rhys’s body. He wasn’t asleep. He was at the bottom of the steps.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_bed.response.0": "…I declined a call. In my sleep. People do.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_bed.response.1": "You tell him what the 999 line heard: someone breathing beside Rhys, two rings of the ‘Small Hours’ riff, then footsteps back up the stone steps and a door closing.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_bed.response.2": "I’d like to speak to a solicitor now, please. I think that’s my right.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_bed.title": "Eddie wasn’t asleep",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_book.insight": "Two brass corners from Rhys’s notebook, one stamped R M, were in the ash of the stove Eddie lit on Sunday morning. He took the book from Rhys’s pocket, and burned it.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_book.response.0": "Eddie looks at the two scorched corners in your hand for a long time.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_book.response.1": "Thirty years of words. Do you know how many of them were mine? None. I just made sure people heard them.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_book.response.2": "He doesn’t say anything else.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_book.title": "The book went into Eddie’s fire",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_happy.insight": "Rhys wasn’t happy with the sale. On Saturday he wrote to PRS to put Dean’s name on ‘Small Hours’, and told Eddie he wasn’t signing on Monday: ‘You’ll sink us both.’",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_happy.response.0": "…All right. He had cold feet on Saturday. They all do, at the last minute, about everything. It’s my job to talk them down.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_happy.response.1": "He’d have signed. Rhys always signed in the end.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_happy.response.2": "And I’ll tell you what I told him: Dean played on that record, he didn’t write it. Thirty years of arguing doesn’t make it true.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_eddie_happy.title": "Rhys wasn’t going to sign",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_freya_asleep.insight": "Freya wasn’t asleep. After the clocks went back she was in the lounge, in view of Huw, cutting the clip, and she saw Rhys leave. She has footage of the paramedics too, which she never gave the police.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_freya_asleep.response.0": "…He could see me. Of course he could.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_freya_asleep.response.1": "I was in the lounge the whole time, cutting the clip, until I heard Carys scream. Huw was at his desk; I could see the back of his head through the side window all night. Rhys came through on his way out and said, ‘Night, Frey,’ and I said night without even looking up.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_freya_asleep.response.2": "And when the ambulance came I filmed it. The paramedics, Carys on the cobbles. I couldn’t stop myself. I didn’t give the police that one.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_freya_asleep.response.3": "She opens the file on her laptop and turns it towards you.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_freya_asleep.title": "Freya was in the lounge",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_freya_sold.insight": "The Banner says it got the video ‘from a member of the documentary crew’, and Freya is the whole crew. She sold the row to the paper before anyone knew Rhys was dead.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_freya_sold.response.0": "… ‘A member of the documentary crew.’ Thanks, lads.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_freya_sold.response.1": "I cut the row into a clip that night and sent it to the Banner’s picture desk. Eight thousand pounds. My company’s broke, and a reunion bust-up is a reunion bust-up. I sent it before — before. I swear I sent it before.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_freya_sold.response.2": "When they ran it on Monday with that headline, I was sick in the lounge bin.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_freya_sold.title": "Freya sold the clip",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_huw_light.insight": "The landing light wasn’t working that night. On Sunday morning Huw found the bulb loose in its holder and twisted it back before the police looked in daylight, to protect his studio.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_huw_light.response.0": "…Duw. All right. It was dark up there. Black as your hat.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_huw_light.response.1": "Sunday morning, eight o’clock, I went up to look, and the bulb was loose in its holder. I thought it had shaken loose. No rail, and a dead light — the insurers would have closed me down and I’d have lost the lot.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_huw_light.response.2": "So I twisted it back before they came to look in the daylight, and told them it had been on all night. I’ve been sick about it since.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_huw_light.title": "The landing was dark",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alibi.conclusion": "Both calls were real, and both were in the first one o’clock. Eddie’s ran from twenty past one to five to two, summer time — 5:20 to 5:55 in Los Angeles — and he went up to bed before the clocks went back. Carys talked to her sister from half five to ten to six, Vancouver time, which that night was half past one to ten to two, summer time. When Rhys fell, at 01:41 the second time round, neither of them had an alibi at all.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alibi.options.0": "Both: Eddie’s and Carys’s calls each ran past 01:41",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alibi.options.1": "Neither: Eddie’s call and Carys’s call were both in the first one o’clock",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alibi.options.2": "Only Carys’s: Vancouver is eight hours behind, so her call came later",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alibi.options.3": "Only Eddie’s: Los Angeles logged his call until 5:55pm",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alibi.proofLabels.0": "When Eddie’s call was",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alibi.proofLabels.1": "When Carys’s call was",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alibi.question": "Whose phone call covered 01:41, the second time round, when Rhys fell?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alibi.title": "Two alibis, one wrong hour",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alive.conclusion": "After the row Rhys went back into the studio and sang Takes 8 and 9, both after the clocks went back. At 01:38, second time round, Huw told the band he had just sung ‘the vocal of his life’. Dean had left him at the steps in the first one o’clock. Rhys was alive, and singing, for more than an hour after the row.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alive.options.0": "Yes: he sang two more takes after the clocks went back",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alive.options.1": "No: he fell within minutes of the row",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alive.options.2": "Yes: he walked on the hill until he fell",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alive.options.3": "Yes, but only until twenty to two, the first time round",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alive.proofLabels.0": "What Rhys did after the row",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alive.proofLabels.1": "Which one o’clock it was",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alive.question": "Was Rhys alive after Dean left him at the steps?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_alive.title": "The vocal of his life",
 "deductions:deductions.d_camera.conclusion": "Freya’s camera never went back: it is still on summer time today, an hour ahead. So its 01:22 is summer time, the first one o’clock. Dean shoved Rhys before the clocks went back — and if Rhys fell at 01:41 the second time round, the row was more than an hour before the fall.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_camera.options.0": "At 01:22 — nineteen minutes before the fall",
 "deductions:deductions.d_camera.options.1": "After the fall: her camera runs an hour slow",
 "deductions:deductions.d_camera.options.2": "In the first one o’clock, before the clocks went back",
 "deductions:deductions.d_camera.options.3": "On Friday night: the clip is from the night before",
 "deductions:deductions.d_camera.proofLabels.0": "What Freya’s camera’s clock is set to",
 "deductions:deductions.d_camera.proofLabels.1": "When the camera says the row was",
 "deductions:deductions.d_camera.question": "When did Freya film Dean shoving Rhys?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_camera.title": "A camera on summer time",
 "deductions:deductions.d_clocks.conclusion": "On Saturday night the clocks went back: at 2 a.m. summer time became 1 a.m. winter time. Every phone and computer at Hafod changed by itself and showed the hour from one to two twice. Take 7, at 01:38, was the first time round; Takes 8 and 9, at 01:06 and 01:24, the second. Anything that wasn’t changed by hand — Freya’s camera, the Aga — kept summer time all night.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_clocks.options.0": "Take 7 was redone at the end and kept its old number",
 "deductions:deductions.d_clocks.options.1": "The computer’s clock jumped when the power flickered in the storm",
 "deductions:deductions.d_clocks.options.2": "Huw typed the times in by hand and got them muddled",
 "deductions:deductions.d_clocks.options.3": "The clocks went back at 2 a.m., so one o’clock came round twice",
 "deductions:deductions.d_clocks.proofLabels.0": "The times that run backwards",
 "deductions:deductions.d_clocks.proofLabels.1": "What happened at two o’clock",
 "deductions:deductions.d_clocks.question": "Why do the times on Huw’s take list run backwards?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_clocks.title": "One o’clock, twice",
 "deductions:deductions.d_fall.conclusion": "Rhys went backwards down the whole flight: his skull was broken at the back, he was grazed by every step, and his phone and his blood are at the very top. The shove on Freya’s video was at the bottom step. Whoever pushed Rhys did it on the landing, fourteen steps above the place where Dean shoved him.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_fall.options.0": "From the bottom step, when Dean shoved him on the video",
 "deductions:deductions.d_fall.options.1": "From the very top: backwards, down all fourteen steps",
 "deductions:deductions.d_fall.options.2": "From halfway up, missing his footing in the dark",
 "deductions:deductions.d_fall.options.3": "He didn’t fall: he was hit on the cobbles",
 "deductions:deductions.d_fall.proofLabels.0": "How he was hurt",
 "deductions:deductions.d_fall.proofLabels.1": "Where the fall began",
 "deductions:deductions.d_fall.question": "Where did Rhys fall from?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_fall.title": "From the top step",
 "deductions:deductions.d_landing.conclusion": "The landing light works perfectly, and stays on a full minute. That night it came on for Eddie, just before the clocks went back, went out almost at once, and never came on again, not even for Rhys. A quarter-turn of the bulb does that, and only from the landing, standing under the light. Somebody turned it at the moment Eddie went up to bed.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_landing.options.0": "Someone on the landing loosened the bulb when the light came on for Eddie",
 "deductions:deductions.d_landing.options.1": "The bulb blew when Eddie went up, and Huw replaced it on Sunday",
 "deductions:deductions.d_landing.options.2": "Freya switched it off at the fuse box in her room",
 "deductions:deductions.d_landing.options.3": "Rhys loosened it himself, because the light woke Carys",
 "deductions:deductions.d_landing.proofLabels.0": "The light as it is now",
 "deductions:deductions.d_landing.proofLabels.1": "The light that night",
 "deductions:deductions.d_landing.question": "Why was the landing dark when Rhys climbed the steps?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_landing.title": "A bulb loosened",
 "deductions:deductions.d_motive.conclusion": "On Saturday afternoon Rhys wrote to PRS to make ‘Small Hours’ Pritchard/Morgan, fifty-fifty, from the beginning, and he meant to do it on Monday — the day the sale of his songs was due, with a promise in it that he was the only writer. Dean had every reason to keep Rhys alive. Somebody else had every reason not to.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_motive.options.0": "Sign the sale of his songs, as planned",
 "deductions:deductions.d_motive.options.1": "Announce the tour",
 "deductions:deductions.d_motive.options.2": "Put Dean’s name beside his own on ‘Small Hours’",
 "deductions:deductions.d_motive.options.3": "Leave the band again",
 "deductions:deductions.d_motive.proofLabels.0": "What Rhys wrote",
 "deductions:deductions.d_motive.proofLabels.1": "Who he told",
 "deductions:deductions.d_motive.question": "What was Rhys going to do on Monday?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_motive.title": "His name on it",
 "deductions:deductions.d_nobody.conclusion": "From quarter past one, after the clocks went back, Bryn sat in his car facing the yard. Dean was asleep inside — Bryn had photographed him at 01:12 — and nobody came out of the farmhouse until Carys ran out after the alarm. Whoever came down to Rhys came down the steps from the granary, and went back up.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_nobody.options.0": "Yes: Dean, once Bryn had gone out to his car",
 "deductions:deductions.d_nobody.options.1": "Yes: Carys, while Bryn was looking at the steps",
 "deductions:deductions.d_nobody.options.2": "Yes: Bryn himself, leaving his car",
 "deductions:deductions.d_nobody.options.3": "No: Bryn watched the door, and nobody came out until Carys",
 "deductions:deductions.d_nobody.proofLabels.0": "Who was watching the farmhouse door",
 "deductions:deductions.d_nobody.proofLabels.1": "Who was inside, and when",
 "deductions:deductions.d_nobody.question": "Could anyone have come out of the farmhouse when Rhys fell?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_nobody.title": "Nobody came out",
 "deductions:deductions.d_ringtone.conclusion": "Two minutes after the fall, the open 999 line heard someone beside Rhys, then a phone ringing with the opening riff of ‘Small Hours’, then footsteps going back up the steps. At that moment — 6.43 in Los Angeles, 01:43 at Hafod — Westwater’s lawyer rang Eddie, and he declined the call. Eddie’s ringtone has been that riff since 1996.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_ringtone.options.0": "Rhys’s own phone, in his pocket",
 "deductions:deductions.d_ringtone.options.1": "Bryn’s, from his car",
 "deductions:deductions.d_ringtone.options.2": "Eddie’s: Los Angeles was ringing him back",
 "deductions:deductions.d_ringtone.options.3": "Carys’s, as the ambulance service rang her",
 "deductions:deductions.d_ringtone.proofLabels.0": "What the 999 line heard",
 "deductions:deductions.d_ringtone.proofLabels.1": "Whose phone plays that riff",
 "deductions:deductions.d_ringtone.question": "Whose phone rang beside Rhys after he fell?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_ringtone.title": "The riff",
 "dialogues:statements.st_bryn_bed.text": "I was in bed by midnight, stone-cold sober, like every night for twelve years.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_bryn_car.text": "From quarter past one, after the clocks went back, I sat in my car with a bottle, facing the yard. Nobody came out of the farmhouse until Carys ran out.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_bryn_dean.text": "After my drums I went over to the farmhouse. Dean had just come in and was on the stairs, too drunk to stand. I got him to bed and sat with him. My phone went back to one o’clock, and a bit after that I sent the chat a photo of him.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_bryn_saw.text": "I saw Rhys go up the steps in the dark. A thump, and an alarm. Then someone came down from the top with a phone lit up and bent over him. A phone rang twice, and they went back up the steps, fast.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_bryn_sleep.text": "After I sent the photo, I went to sleep.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_bryn_tour.text": "On Friday Rhys told me that one drink and I was off the tour.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_bryn_watch.text": "Everybody knew that if Rhys fell, his watch rang 999 by itself. It did in June, at a gig.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_carys_call.text": "I was on the phone to my sister until about ten to two. Then I took a sleeping tablet and slept until the ambulance people rang.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_carys_eddieloan.text": "Eddie told me he’d borrowed £400,000 against the sale himself, on his house. If Monday went wrong, he’d lose it.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_carys_fine.text": "Rhys and I didn’t argue. I slept in the farmhouse because he snores.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_carys_loan.text": "In April Eddie lent me £60,000, to be paid back out of the sale.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_carys_nodebt.text": "I don’t owe anybody anything.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_carys_row.text": "On Saturday afternoon Rhys told me he was giving Dean half of ‘Small Hours’. I told him he was mad, and moved my bag to the farmhouse.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_carys_sister.text": "My sister says we spoke from half five to ten to six, her time, in Vancouver.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_dean_book.text": "Rhys never went anywhere without his notebook — black, with brass on the corners. Every word he ever wrote is in it.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_dean_left.text": "Rhys and I argued at the bottom of the steps. I left him there alive at about quarter to two and went to bed.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_dean_notsong.text": "We weren’t arguing about the song. Just the take — my playing.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_dean_promise.text": "In the yard Rhys told me he was putting my name on ‘Small Hours’ on Monday. I called him a liar.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_dean_steps.text": "I never set foot on the granary steps all week.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_dean_wrote.text": "I wrote the music of ‘Small Hours’ in my kitchen in Pill in March 1995. Rhys wrote the words that night.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_eddie_bed.text": "After my call I went straight to bed and slept until Carys screamed.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_eddie_book.text": "I never touched Rhys’s notebook. I couldn’t tell you where it is.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_eddie_call.text": "From twenty past one until five to two I was on a video call to Los Angeles, on the control-room sofa, with Huw right in front of me.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_eddie_coldfeet.text": "On Saturday Rhys got cold feet about the sale. Artists do. He’d have signed.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_eddie_happy.text": "Rhys was happy with the sale. He’d have signed on Monday.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_eddie_ringtone.text": "The riff of ‘Small Hours’ has been my ringtone since 1996.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_eddie_share.text": "My company has had a quarter of the publishing on Halflight’s songs since 1995.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_eddie_watch.text": "I knew Rhys’s watch rang 999 by itself. In June I had to ring the ambulance service to apologise.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_freya_asleep.text": "I went up to my room at about two and slept straight through until the screaming.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_freya_clock.text": "I never touch the clock on my camera.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_freya_heard.text": "On Saturday afternoon I heard Carys shouting at Rhys in the granary: ‘You’re giving away half of everything for a guilty conscience!’",
 "dialogues:statements.st_freya_light.text": "When Eddie went up to bed, just before the clocks went back, the landing light came on and went straight off again. After that it never came on again, not even when Rhys went across to bed.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_freya_lounge.text": "After the clocks went back I was in the lounge cutting the clip, with Huw at his desk through the side window, until I heard Carys scream. Rhys said goodnight to me a few minutes before that, and went out.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_freya_nosale.text": "I never sold anything to anyone. The police must have leaked the clip.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_freya_sold.text": "I cut the row into a clip that night and sold it to the Banner for £8,000.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_huw_bulb.text": "On Sunday morning I found the landing bulb loose in its holder and twisted it back, before the police looked in daylight.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_huw_desk.text": "I was at the desk all night, start to finish.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_huw_glass.text": "While Rhys sang his last takes, Freya was in the lounge on her laptop. I could see her through the glass the whole time.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_huw_light.text": "The landing light was working all night. Those steps are perfectly safe.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_huw_overheard.text": "On Saturday at half five I heard Rhys tell Eddie, ‘I’m not signing on Monday. Half of “Small Hours” is Dean’s.’ Eddie said, ‘You’ll sink us both.’",
 "dialogues:statements.st_huw_sequence.text": "Eddie was on his call through Bryn’s drums, Take 7, then said goodnight and went up, before we started Rhys’s vocals, Takes 8 and 9.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_huw_stove.text": "At half seven on Sunday morning Eddie lit the wood burner in the lounge, and sat by it for an hour.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_dean.lines.0": "Gone. Couldn’t stand. I had to take his boots off for him, like a toddler. I sat with him in case he was sick in his sleep — you learn that, in the rooms.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_dean.lines.1": "He wasn’t going anywhere, I’ll tell you that. He couldn’t have found the door.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_dean.prompt": "What state was Dean in?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_night.lines.0": "Bryn, where were you on Saturday night?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_night.lines.1": "In bed by midnight. Lemonade and decaf, like every night for twelve years. I did my drums early and left them to it. Old men need their sleep.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_night.prompt": "Where were you on Saturday night?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_rhys.lines.0": "Best mate since I was sixteen. Best man at both my weddings — I’d have asked him to a third if I’d had one.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_rhys.lines.1": "He read me the riot act on Friday, mind. He’d seen me eyeing the wine at dinner. ‘One drink, Bryn, and you’re off the tour. I’m not losing you again.’ Fair play. He was right.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_rhys.lines.2": "It was like 1996 all over again this week. Same jokes, same rows. Our riff’s on half the phones in the place — Eddie’s had it as his ringtone for thirty years, the soft old sod, and Carys put it on hers this summer. Every time a phone goes off, I’m nineteen.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_rhys.prompt": "How did you get on with Rhys?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_watch.lines.0": "Ha — yes. In June, at a solo gig of his in Cardiff. He jumped off the front of the stage, landed on his backside, and two minutes later there’s an ambulance outside asking for him. His watch had done it on its own.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_watch.lines.1": "We pulled his leg about it all week. Everybody knew — if Rhys fell over, his watch rang 999 and told them exactly when and where.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_watch.prompt": "His watch rang 999 by itself. Had that happened before?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_who.lines.0": "I couldn’t see a face. Just somebody coming down the steps with a phone lit up, bending over him, and then going back up, quick, the way they’d come. A phone rang while they were down there — some tune, I couldn’t tell you what over the wind and that alarm.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_who.lines.1": "Not from the farmhouse, I know that much — I’d been staring at that door all night. Whoever it was came down from the top, and went back up there.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_who.prompt": "Who did you see at the steps?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_why.lines.0": "Because I’d have had to tell them what I was doing in my car at that time of night. Twelve years. My sponsor, my kids, the tour. Rhys had told me, one drink.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_why.lines.1": "And then he was dead, and I thought — I can’t have seen what I saw. I was drunk. It was dark. I kept my mouth shut and hated myself for it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_bryn_why.prompt": "Why didn’t you tell the police?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_eddie.lines.0": "Eddie’s been living on the sale since the spring. The house in Highgate, the reunion, the film — he paid for most of it up front.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_eddie.lines.1": "He said the bank had lent him four hundred thousand against it, on his house. ‘If Monday goes wrong, Carys, we’re both on the street.’ I thought he was joking.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_eddie.prompt": "Tell me about Eddie’s money.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_emails.lines.0": "Eddie copies me in on everything. I haven’t opened a single one since Sunday.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_emails.lines.1": "She unlocks her phone and hands it to you. Near the top, unopened, is an email from Westwater’s lawyer in Los Angeles, sent at 03:12 on Sunday morning.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_emails.prompt": "May I see the emails about the sale?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_night.lines.0": "Mrs Morgan, where were you on Saturday night?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_night.lines.1": "In the spare room in the farmhouse. I was on the phone to my sister in Vancouver until about ten to two, then I took a sleeping tablet. The next thing I knew, the ambulance people were ringing me to say Rhys had fallen.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_night.lines.2": "I ran out in my socks. He was at the bottom of the steps. I’ve told the police all of this.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_night.prompt": "Where were you on Saturday night?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_rhys.lines.0": "When I met him he’d been sober for a year and he was terrified of everything: of his own songs, of being happy. I ran his life for seven years so he could just write.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_rhys.lines.1": "And this year, when ‘Small Hours’ came back, I watched him become himself again. Do you know what that’s like, and then this?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_rhys.prompt": "Tell me about Rhys.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_room.lines.0": "He snores. It’s no more interesting than that. We didn’t argue, if that’s what you’ve heard. We never argued.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_room.prompt": "Why were you sleeping in the farmhouse?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_sale.lines.0": "A fund in Los Angeles, Westwater, buying everything: Rhys’s songs and Eddie’s quarter of the publishing. It was meant to be signed on Monday. On Saturday Rhys told me he was going to wreck it, and now it’ll go through with my name on it instead. You can imagine how that looks.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_sale.lines.1": "The papers are in my room in the farmhouse. Look at them, if it helps. I’m past caring who reads what.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_sale.prompt": "Tell me about the sale.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_sister.lines.0": "About half one until ten to two. I looked at the time when I put the phone down, because I was going to take a tablet.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_sister.lines.1": "My sister says it was half five till ten to six, her time, in Vancouver. Why does that matter?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_sister.prompt": "When exactly were you on the phone to your sister?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_will.lines.0": "I do. I’m his wife. The sale goes ahead on the same terms, Eddie says; the lawyers are already talking.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_will.lines.1": "And before you ask: I don’t owe anybody anything. I don’t need his money.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_carys_will.prompt": "Who inherits Rhys’s songs?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_eddie.lines.0": "Eddie found us in the Riverside in ’94 and signed us on a beer mat. He’s been in the middle of everything since. The money, the forms, the story everyone tells.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_eddie.lines.1": "When I left, he was the one who rang me every Christmas. ‘All right, Deano? Keeping off it?’ I always thought he felt bad about the forms.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_eddie.prompt": "Tell me about Eddie.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_night.lines.0": "Dean, tell me about Saturday night.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_night.lines.1": "Long session. Six takes of the new one, all of us, and I was drinking through every one of them. I’m not proud of it. I was rough on six — you can hear it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_night.lines.2": "We went out for a smoke and had a row at the bottom of the steps — you’ve seen it, the whole country’s seen it. I shoved him. He fell back against the bottom step and got up again, shaking his head at me.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_night.lines.3": "I left him there alive, about quarter to two, and went to bed. Next thing I know there’s a copper shaking me and the yard’s full of blue lights.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_night.prompt": "Tell me about Saturday night.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_police.lines.0": "Because I woke up with a copper’s torch in my face and Rhys was dead and the last thing I’d done was put my hands on him. What would you have said?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_police.lines.1": "I’ve told them the truth since. They just don’t like it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_police.prompt": "Why did you lie to the police?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_rhys.lines.0": "We met in school, in Pill. Fifteen. He had a bass he couldn’t play and a notebook full of words, and I had a guitar and no words at all. That was the band, really. Everything after was just more people.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_rhys.lines.1": "That notebook. In ’94 he copied everything worth keeping into a new one — black, brass on the corners — and he never went anywhere without it after. Every word he cared about is in that book. Every word of ‘Small Hours’.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_rhys.prompt": "What was Rhys to you?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_shove.lines.0": "Because I was drunk and he was standing there being reasonable. We weren’t even arguing about the song. Just the take — my playing. He said six was rough and I took it badly.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_shove.prompt": "Why did you shove him?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_song.lines.0": "I wrote the music. The riff, the chords, the bit where it lifts into the chorus. March ’95, in my kitchen in Pill, on a guitar with five strings. Rhys wrote the words that same night, on the end of my table.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_song.lines.1": "Eddie did the forms. ‘One name looks better on a sleeve, we’ll sort it out later.’ Later never came. I’ve had twenty-eight years of later.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_song.lines.2": "There’s a tape. Ffion knows where it is. Go on, play it — you’ll see.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_song.prompt": "Who wrote ‘Small Hours’?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_steps.lines.0": "Never. I never set foot on them steps all week — I was in the farmhouse. I left him at the bottom, with a cigarette, and I went to bed.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_steps.lines.1": "Fourteen steps, no rail, wet as a fish. I said on the first day somebody’d break their neck on them.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_dean_steps.prompt": "Did you go up the steps after him?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_book.lines.0": "His book? I wouldn’t know. I never touched it in thirty years — nobody did. Probably in his jacket, or the police have it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_book.prompt": "Where is Rhys’s notebook?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_clocks.lines.0": "Everybody knew. Huw had it on the whiteboard in letters a foot high. I told him on my way out, ‘There’s your extra hour, Huw.’",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_clocks.lines.1": "Why?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_clocks.prompt": "Did you know the clocks were going back that night?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_night.lines.0": "Mr Cole, where were you when Rhys fell?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_night.lines.1": "On a video call to Los Angeles, on the control-room sofa, from twenty past one until five to two. The people buying the songs. Huw was sat right there in front of me — ask him.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_night.lines.2": "Then I went straight up to bed and slept like the dead until Carys screamed. God forgive me, I slept through it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_night.prompt": "Where were you when Rhys fell?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_rhys.lines.0": "The Riverside in Newport, 1994. Three lads who couldn’t play, and one of them could sing like it hurt. I signed them on a beer mat. I’ve still got the beer mat.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_rhys.lines.1": "Thirty years. I got him off the drink twice. He was my boy.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_rhys.prompt": "Tell me about Rhys.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_ringtone.lines.0": "My ringtone? The riff. ‘Small Hours’. Has been since 1996 — the boys hate it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_ringtone.lines.1": "Why do you ask?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_ringtone.prompt": "What’s your ringtone, Mr Cole?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_sale.lines.0": "Westwater, in LA: six point two million for the catalogue. My company’s had a quarter of the publishing since ’95 — everybody knows that. It was due to sign on Monday.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_sale.lines.1": "Rhys was happy with it. Over the moon. He’d have signed on Monday, and the boys would’ve had a tour, and I’d have retired to the seaside. That was the plan.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_sale.prompt": "Tell me about the sale.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_song.lines.0": "I did the forms, in ’95, the way you did then. Rhys wrote the song; Dean played on it. Everybody plays on everything. If we’d put every name on that sleeve we’d have needed a bigger sleeve.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_song.lines.1": "Dean’s had a chip on his shoulder about it ever since. You’ve seen where that got him.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_song.prompt": "Who registered ‘Small Hours’?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_watch.lines.0": "The ambulance in June? Who didn’t. I was the one who had to ring them and apologise. ‘He’s fine, he’s a singer, he fell off a stage.’",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_watch.lines.1": "God. If it had gone off like that on Saturday and he’d just been sitting on the cobbles with a sore head…",
 "dialogues:topics.t_eddie_watch.prompt": "Did you know about Rhys’s watch?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_banner.lines.0": "Not from me. I gave everything to the police on Sunday. Somebody there must have leaked it — it happens all the time.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_banner.lines.1": "I never sold anything to anyone.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_banner.prompt": "How did the Banner get your footage?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_film.lines.0": "Halflight, twenty-six years on: three men in a room with everything they never said. That was the pitch, and it was working. I’m the whole crew — camera, sound, the lot. Then Saturday.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_film.lines.1": "The streaming people rang on Monday. They want ‘the night itself’. They’ve doubled the budget. I haven’t decided whether to be sick.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_film.prompt": "Tell me about your film.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_kit.lines.0": "It’s on the windowsill in my room, charging. Help yourself.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_kit.lines.1": "I’ve no idea what time it thinks it is, by the way. I never touch the clock on that thing — I just point it and shoot.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_kit.prompt": "May I look at your camera?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_night.lines.0": "Freya, where were you on Saturday night?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_night.lines.1": "I filmed until the row, and wrapped not long after. I went up to my room at about two and slept straight through, until the screaming.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_night.prompt": "Where were you on Saturday night?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_rhys.lines.0": "Dreadful. He forgot the camera was there, so everything he did was usable. On Thursday he did twenty minutes about Dean, looking straight at the lens, and then said ‘Not that bit, Frey,’ and I said fine.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_rhys.lines.1": "I’ve still got it. I haven’t watched it again.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_rhys.prompt": "What was Rhys like to film?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_saturday.lines.0": "Rhys and Carys, about half past two. The walls up there are paper; the whole landing heard. Not words, mostly — voices. Then her: ‘You’re giving away half of everything for a guilty conscience!’ And then her bag bumping down the steps past my door.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_saturday.lines.1": "She went to sleep in the farmhouse after that. Everyone pretended not to notice.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_saturday.prompt": "Did you hear anything on Saturday afternoon?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_thursday.lines.0": "The bit he told me not to use. I’ve never cut it into anything. Here — the whole thing.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_thursday.lines.1": "She finds the file on her laptop and turns it towards you.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_thursday.prompt": "May I see what Rhys said about Dean on Thursday?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_window.lines.0": "The steps. From my end of the sofa you look straight across the yard at them, like a stage.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_window.lines.1": "When Eddie went up to bed, just before the clocks went back, the landing light came on the way it does — and went off again almost at once. It usually stays on a whole minute. I remember thinking it had broken.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_window.lines.2": "After that it never came on again. Not when Rhys went across to bed, either. He walked out into the dark and I lost him, and I thought, he’ll break his neck on those steps. Then I put my headphones back on and went back to my clip. I didn’t look up again until Carys screamed.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_freya_window.prompt": "What could you see from the lounge window?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_glass.lines.0": "Only Freya, in the lounge next door. I could see her through the side window the whole time Rhys was singing: on the sofa with her laptop and her headphones on, cutting something.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_glass.lines.1": "Rhys left a few minutes after Take 9. ‘Night, Huw.’ I stayed and backed everything up. I never heard a thing. That room’s built so you can’t.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_glass.prompt": "Who else was in the studio after the clocks went back?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_rhys.lines.0": "He made his first record here when he was twenty-two, and slept on that sofa because he couldn’t afford the granary. This week I gave him the best room up there. He said, ‘Look at us, Huw. We’ve come up in the world.’",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_rhys.prompt": "Tell me about Rhys.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_saturday.lines.0": "Half past five. I was setting up, with my headphones on, and somebody had left the talkback open in the lounge. Rhys’s voice: ‘I’m not signing on Monday, Eddie. Half of “Small Hours” is Dean’s.’",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_saturday.lines.1": "And Eddie: ‘You’ll sink us both.’ Then the door went, and I took my headphones off and pretended I’d never heard it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_saturday.prompt": "Did anything happen on Saturday, before the session?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_sequence.lines.0": "Eddie was on his call all the way through Bryn’s drums — Take 7. Headphones on, thumbs up from the sofa. When it finished he said goodnight and went up to bed. ‘There’s your extra hour, Huw,’ he said.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_sequence.lines.1": "That was before we’d even started Rhys’s vocals, Takes 8 and 9. Rhys sang them to me and nobody else.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_sequence.prompt": "Who left the control room that night, and when?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_session.lines.0": "Mr Bevan, tell me about Saturday’s session.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_session.lines.1": "Nine takes of ‘Holding Pattern’. Six with the whole band, then Bryn’s drums again on their own, then two vocals from Rhys. The last one — duw, the last one. I’ve been doing this forty-five years.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_session.lines.2": "I was at the desk all night, start to finish. It’s all on the computer, every take; have a look. And the band’s iPad is in the lounge, if you want their chat. I’ll unlock it for you.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_session.prompt": "Tell me about Saturday’s session.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_steps.lines.0": "They’ve stood four hundred years without one. The insurers wanted a rail and a light, and I put the light in, in June — a good one, on a sensor.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_steps.lines.1": "And it was working all night, before you ask. Those steps are perfectly safe if you look where you’re going.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_steps.prompt": "Those granary steps have no handrail.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_sunday.lines.0": "Nobody slept. The last police car went about seven. At half past, Eddie came into the lounge and lit the wood burner — said he was freezing. First log I’d seen him lift all week. He sat by it for an hour.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_sunday.lines.1": "I haven’t cleaned the stove since. The police told me not to touch anything, and then they never came back.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_huw_sunday.prompt": "What happened on Sunday morning?",
 "evidence:evidence.aga_clock.detail": "The cream Aga in the farmhouse kitchen has a small clock on its front. It says 15:41. Your watch says 14:41.\n\n‘Nobody’s done the Aga,’ Huw says. ‘Nobody ever does the Aga till Christmas.’",
 "evidence:evidence.aga_clock.name": "The Aga’s clock",
 "evidence:evidence.aga_clock.summary": "Still an hour fast. Nobody has put it back.",
 "evidence:evidence.band_chat.detail": "The band’s group chat, ‘HALFLIGHT 💡’, on the lounge iPad. Saturday night into Sunday, in the order the messages arrived:\n\n22:14 Freya: [photo: the three of them round one microphone] The boys are back 💡\n00:48 Huw: Take 6 in the bag. Tea in the lounge if anyone’s still alive.\n01:52 Freya: Wrapping for tonight. Got some gold 🎬\n01:12 Bryn: [photo: Dean asleep in his clothes, hugging a bucket] Rock and roll 🤘\n01:38 Huw: Rhys has just sung the vocal of his life. Bed 🌙",
 "evidence:evidence.band_chat.name": "The band chat",
 "evidence:evidence.band_chat.summary": "In order: Freya at 01:52; then Bryn’s photo at 01:12; then Huw at 01:38.",
 "evidence:evidence.bryn_bottle.detail": "Bryn’s old estate car is still parked a few metres from the farmhouse porch, nose towards the granary steps. In the glovebox, under the road atlas, there’s a half-litre bottle of vodka, two-thirds gone, and a packet of extra-strong mints. The driver’s window has been left open an inch.",
 "evidence:evidence.bryn_bottle.name": "The bottle in Bryn’s car",
 "evidence:evidence.bryn_bottle.summary": "Vodka, two-thirds gone, hidden in his glovebox.",
 "evidence:evidence.bulb.detail": "Huw takes the cage off the landing light for you. Inside is a plain bayonet bulb. Give it a quarter-turn and it sits loose and dark in its holder, and the sensor clicks uselessly. A quarter-turn back and the landing floods with light again.\n\nAnyone standing on the landing, reaching up, could do it in a second. Nobody climbing the steps could do it without lighting them up first.",
 "evidence:evidence.bulb.name": "The landing bulb",
 "evidence:evidence.bulb.summary": "A quarter-turn and it sits loose and dark; anyone on the landing could do it in a second.",
 "evidence:evidence.carys_loan.detail": "Also in Carys’s folder, a loan agreement dated 12 April 2024: Cole Music Ltd lends Mrs Carys Morgan £60,000, interest-free, ‘repayable in full from the proceeds of the Westwater completion’. Signed by Eddie Cole and Carys Morgan.",
 "evidence:evidence.carys_loan.name": "Carys’s loan from Eddie",
 "evidence:evidence.carys_loan.summary": "April 2024: Eddie’s company lent Carys £60,000, to be repaid from the sale.",
 "evidence:evidence.clasp.detail": "The ash pan of the lounge’s wood burner hasn’t been emptied since Sunday. Among the ash and the charred ends of logs are two small brass corners, the kind that protect the corners of an old-fashioned hardback notebook. They’re scorched black, and one has ‘R M’ punched into it. There’s a curl of burnt card between them.",
 "evidence:evidence.clasp.name": "Brass corners in the ash",
 "evidence:evidence.clasp.summary": "From the lounge stove: two scorched brass corners from a notebook, one stamped ‘R M’.",
 "evidence:evidence.dana_email.detail": "On Carys’s phone, an email she was copied on and never opened. From Dana Whitlock, Westwater Song Partners, Los Angeles, to Eddie Cole. Sent Sunday 27 October, 03:12 (Saturday 20:12 in Los Angeles):\n\n‘Eddie — great call tonight, and thanks for moving it to suit your side. Tried you at 6.43 our time to confirm Monday’s signing. You declined, so I’m assuming you’d crashed! Completion docs attached.\nFor the file: tonight’s call, Sat 26 Oct, 5:20–5:55pm PT, Eddie Cole for the Morgan side.\nDana’",
 "evidence:evidence.dana_email.name": "Email from Westwater’s lawyer",
 "evidence:evidence.dana_email.summary": "‘Tried you at 6.43 our time… you declined.’ The call itself: 5:20–5:55pm Pacific.",
 "evidence:evidence.dean_tape.detail": "A cassette in a cracked case on Dean’s shelf, labelled in faded biro: ‘SMALL HOURS — D’s tune — Pill, 3/95’.\n\nFfion plays it on Dean’s old deck. A guitar, alone: the riff the whole world knows, three times over, slower than the record. Then a young man’s voice, laughing: ‘That’s it, Deano. That’s the one. Write it down before you lose it.’\n\nDean says nothing at all. Ffion says that voice is Rhys.",
 "evidence:evidence.dean_tape.name": "The cassette from 1995",
 "evidence:evidence.dean_tape.summary": "Dean playing the riff alone; then Rhys’s voice: ‘That’s it, Deano. That’s the one.’",
 "evidence:evidence.freya_camera.detail": "Freya’s main camera, charging on the windowsill of her room at the top of the granary steps. Its little screen shows the date and the time: ‘WED 30 OCT 15:12’.\n\nYour watch says 14:12.",
 "evidence:evidence.freya_camera.name": "Freya’s camera",
 "evidence:evidence.freya_camera.summary": "Its clock still reads an hour ahead: it’s still on summer time.",
 "evidence:evidence.insurer_letter.detail": "In Huw’s desk drawer, a letter from Hafod’s insurers, March 2024: ‘Following our survey, cover for the guest accommodation is conditional on (1) a handrail to the external granary steps and (2) lighting to the landing, both by 30 June 2024.’\n\nIn the margin, in Huw’s hand: ‘LIGHT DONE 12/6. Rail — after the band.’",
 "evidence:evidence.insurer_letter.name": "The insurers’ letter",
 "evidence:evidence.insurer_letter.summary": "Cover for the granary depends on a handrail and a landing light. Only the light is done.",
 "evidence:evidence.landing_light.detail": "A caged bulkhead light on the granary wall above the landing, on a motion sensor. Put a foot on the top step and it floods the landing and half the yard with white light, and stays on for a full minute.\n\nYou try it three times. It works perfectly. There’s no handrail on the landing either: it simply stops at the edge.",
 "evidence:evidence.landing_light.name": "The landing light",
 "evidence:evidence.landing_light.summary": "A sensor light over the landing. It works perfectly now, and stays on a full minute.",
 "evidence:evidence.letter_impression.detail": "Huw’s notepad on the lounge table has ‘HAFOD STUDIOS’ at the top of every sheet. The top sheet is blank, but the low sun from the window shows dents in it. You shade it lightly with a pencil, and Rhys’s handwriting comes up white:\n\n‘To PRS for Music. Small Hours (Morgan), 1996.\nI am registered as the only writer of this song. I wasn’t. The music is Dean Pritchard’s: he wrote it in his kitchen in Pill in March 1995, and I wrote the words that night. Please amend the registration to Pritchard/Morgan, 50/50, from first publication.\nI’m sorry it has taken thirty years.\nRhys Morgan, Hafod, 26.10.24’",
 "evidence:evidence.letter_impression.name": "The dents on Huw’s notepad",
 "evidence:evidence.letter_impression.summary": "A letter to PRS in Rhys’s hand: put Dean’s name on ‘Small Hours’, 50/50.",
 "evidence:evidence.lyric_sheet.detail": "The lyric sheet for ‘Holding Pattern’ on the stand in the vocal booth, ringed by a coffee cup and covered in Rhys’s pencil: words crossed out, a breath mark, an arrow. At the bottom, in the same pencil: ‘T9 ✓✓ — that’s the one. Bed. R.’",
 "evidence:evidence.lyric_sheet.name": "The lyric sheet",
 "evidence:evidence.lyric_sheet.summary": "Rhys’s pencil, at the bottom: ‘T9 ✓✓ — that’s the one. Bed. R.’",
 "evidence:evidence.nine_nine_nine.detail": "The ambulance service’s recording of the automated 999 call from Rhys Morgan’s watch, transcribed for the defence. Sunday 27 October 2024. Times are GMT, after the clocks went back.\n\n01:42:05 — Call connects. Automated voice: ‘This is an automated emergency call from a watch. The owner has had a hard fall and is not responding.’ The location follows: Hafod, near Rhayader.\n01:42:30 — Call handler: ‘Ambulance service. Can you hear me? If you can hear me, make a noise.’ No reply. Wind.\n01:42:50 — Footsteps on stone, coming down, quickly. Then, very close: breathing, and a rustle of clothing.\n01:43:10 — A mobile phone rings, very close. The ringtone is an electric guitar riff: the opening bars of ‘Small Hours’. Two rings, then it stops.\n01:43:20 — Footsteps going up stone steps, fast. 01:43:24 — A door closes, above.\n01:45:00 — The call handler rings the emergency contact, Mrs C. Morgan.\n01:46:40 — A woman’s voice, far off and coming closer: ‘Rhys? RHYS!’\n01:46:58 — The same woman, beside the watch, sobbing. Call handler: ‘Hello? Is someone with him?’",
 "evidence:evidence.nine_nine_nine.name": "The 999 recording",
 "evidence:evidence.nine_nine_nine.summary": "After the fall: someone by the watch, a phone ringing a guitar riff at 01:43, then steps going up.",
 "evidence:evidence.paramedic_footage.detail": "A clip Freya never gave the police, file HOLT_0347, timecode 03:16:40 to 03:19:55.\n\nBlue lights swing across the yard. Two paramedics run to the foot of the granary steps, where Carys is kneeling. Eddie Cole stands three steps up in a dressing gown, lighting the scene with his phone. Above him the top of the steps and the landing are black: no light at all.",
 "evidence:evidence.paramedic_footage.name": "Freya’s footage of the paramedics",
 "evidence:evidence.paramedic_footage.summary": "Timecode 03:16: the ambulance arriving. The landing above is pitch dark.",
 "evidence:evidence.police_summary.detail": "Dyfed-Powys Police — summary disclosed to Mr D. Pritchard’s solicitor.\n\nSaturday 26 / Sunday 27 October 2024, Hafod Studios, near Rhayader.\nThe deceased, Rhys MORGAN (52), and Dean PRITCHARD (52) argued at the foot of the granary steps. Video recorded by Ms F. HOLT (camera timecode 01:18–01:26) shows PRITCHARD shouting and pushing MORGAN in the chest.\nPRITCHARD first said he went to bed ‘at about one’ and did not see MORGAN after the session. Shown the video, he said they argued and he left MORGAN ‘alive, at about quarter to two’.\n01:41 — MORGAN’s smartwatch detects a hard fall. 01:42 — the watch makes an automated 999 call.\nMrs C. MORGAN, woken by the ambulance service’s call to her as his emergency contact, found her husband at the foot of the steps.\n02:16 — Ambulance on scene. 02:31 — MORGAN pronounced dead.\n\nNo one else was in the yard. Mr E. COLE was on a video call to Los Angeles in the control room, with Mr H. BEVAN, until about 01:55. Mrs MORGAN was on the telephone to her sister in Canada in the farmhouse until about 01:50, then asleep. Ms HOLT and Mr B. LEWIS were asleep. The landing light at the top of the steps was working when tested. All times are taken from the deceased’s watch, the video’s timecode and the witnesses’ phones.\n\nWorking theory: after the argument shown on video, PRITCHARD followed MORGAN up the steps and pushed him.\nPRITCHARD arrested on suspicion of murder, 27 October; released on police bail, 29 October, pending a charging decision by the CPS.",
 "evidence:evidence.police_summary.name": "Police summary",
 "evidence:evidence.police_summary.summary": "Dyfed-Powys Police’s account of the night, and why they arrested Dean.",
 "evidence:evidence.post_mortem.detail": "Summary of the Home Office pathologist’s findings, sent to Dean’s solicitor:\n\nInjuries consistent with a fall backwards down a full flight of stone steps: a fracture at the back of the skull, and grazing down the back, shoulders and backs of the arms from the edges of the steps.\nA fresh bruise across the breastbone, consistent with a forceful push with both hands shortly before death.\nNo injuries suggesting a struggle.\nNo alcohol or drugs in the blood.\nDeath within minutes of the fall.",
 "evidence:evidence.post_mortem.name": "Post-mortem summary",
 "evidence:evidence.post_mortem.summary": "A fall backwards down the whole flight; a bruise from a two-handed push; no alcohol.",
 "evidence:evidence.rhys_interview.detail": "From Freya’s hard drive: the interview Rhys asked her not to use, Thursday 24 October. Rhys sits on the lounge sofa and looks straight into the lens.\n\n‘There’s something I’ve got to put right about “Small Hours”, before anyone buys it off me. Dean knows what I mean. I told Eddie this morning. He went white as that wall. He said, “Let’s not do anything daft before the weekend. We’ll talk on Saturday.”’\n\nA pause. ‘Not that bit, Frey.’ The clip ends.",
 "evidence:evidence.rhys_interview.name": "Rhys’s Thursday interview",
 "evidence:evidence.rhys_interview.summary": "Rhys to camera, Thursday: ‘I told Eddie this morning… We’ll talk on Saturday.’",
 "evidence:evidence.rhys_room.detail": "The end room on the granary landing, as the police left it. The bed hasn’t been slept in. His bass lies in its open case; his reading glasses are on the windowsill; his jacket hangs on the back of the door, its pockets empty — the police took his wallet.\n\nEveryone you speak to says Rhys never went anywhere without his notebook. It isn’t here, it wasn’t on him, and it isn’t on the police’s list.",
 "evidence:evidence.rhys_room.name": "Rhys’s room",
 "evidence:evidence.rhys_room.summary": "The bed not slept in. No sign of the notebook he always carried.",
 "evidence:evidence.sale_agreement.detail": "In Carys’s folder: the draft agreement for the sale of the Halflight songs to Westwater Song Partners, Los Angeles.\n\nCompletion: Monday 28 October 2024.\nPrice: £6,200,000, for Rhys Morgan’s share as writer, and the quarter share of the publishing held by Cole Music Ltd (director: E. Cole).\nClause 7.2: ‘The Writer is the sole author of every Composition. No other person has claimed, or may claim, authorship of any Composition.’\n\nSigned by Westwater. Not yet signed by Rhys.",
 "evidence:evidence.sale_agreement.name": "The sale agreement",
 "evidence:evidence.sale_agreement.summary": "£6.2 million on Monday, for Rhys’s songs and Cole Music’s quarter; Rhys warrants he’s the sole author.",
 "evidence:evidence.steps_scene.detail": "Fourteen stone steps up the outside wall of the granary to a small landing, worn hollow in the middle, greasy with moss, with no handrail. The police’s markers are still chalked on them.\n\nRhys’s blood is on the edge of the second step from the top, and again lower down. His phone was found face down on the landing, its screen cracked. At the foot, where he landed, the cobbles are darker than the rest.\n\nThe bottom of the steps, where Dean shoved him on the video, is fourteen steps below the place where the blood begins.",
 "evidence:evidence.steps_scene.name": "The granary steps",
 "evidence:evidence.steps_scene.summary": "Fourteen stone steps, no rail. His blood on the second step from the top; his phone on the landing.",
 "evidence:evidence.tabloid_page.detail": "The Daily Banner, Monday 28 October. Front page: ‘THE SHOVE’.\n\nThree stills from a video, with the camera’s timecode in the corner of each: 01:22:09, 01:22:11, 01:22:14. Dean Pritchard with his fist up and his mouth open; then both his hands in Rhys Morgan’s chest; then Rhys stumbling back against the bottom of the granary steps.\n\n‘In the clip, Pritchard can be heard shouting “Thirty years! Thirty years!” … Pritchard claims he co-wrote the band’s hit “Small Hours”. Last year he told a podcast: “He stole my life.” … The Banner obtained the video from a member of the documentary crew.’",
 "evidence:evidence.tabloid_page.name": "The Banner’s front page",
 "evidence:evidence.tabloid_page.summary": "‘THE SHOVE’: stills from Freya’s video, timecode 01:22, and ‘thirty years’.",
 "evidence:evidence.take_list.detail": "The studio computer’s list of takes for ‘Holding Pattern’, Saturday night into Sunday. It numbers the takes in the order they were recorded, and shows the time each one began.\n\nTake 1 · 21:12 · whole band\nTake 2 · 21:48 · whole band\nTake 3 · 22:31 · whole band\nTake 4 · 23:15 · whole band\nTake 5 · 23:58 · whole band\nTake 6 · 00:40 · whole band — ‘D. rough’\nTake 7 · 01:38 · drums only (Bryn)\nTake 8 · 01:06 · lead vocal (Rhys)\nTake 9 · 01:24 · lead vocal (Rhys) — ‘★ KEEPER’",
 "evidence:evidence.take_list.name": "Huw’s take list",
 "evidence:evidence.take_list.summary": "Take 7 at 01:38, then Take 8 at 01:06, and Take 9, Rhys’s keeper, at 01:24.",
 "evidence:evidence.whiteboard.detail": "The whiteboard in the control room, in Huw’s capitals:\n\n‘SAT 26 OCT — NIGHT SESSION — “HOLDING PATTERN”\nCLOCKS GO BACK 2AM = 1AM AGAIN = EXTRA HOUR OF STUDIO TIME!! 😎\n(Computers & phones do it themselves. Wall clock, cameras, the Aga & your cars: BY HAND.)’",
 "evidence:evidence.whiteboard.name": "The studio whiteboard",
 "evidence:evidence.whiteboard.summary": "‘CLOCKS GO BACK 2AM — EXTRA HOUR! Computers & phones do it themselves.’",
 "suspects:suspects.bryn.bio": "Halflight’s drummer, and the one who kept in touch with everybody. A driving instructor in Newport, twelve years sober, with the coin to prove it. He shared a room in the farmhouse with Dean.",
 "suspects:suspects.bryn.dismissal": "Sorry — what’s that got to do with anything?",
 "suspects:suspects.bryn.name": "Bryn Lewis",
 "suspects:suspects.bryn.rebuttal": "Rhys was my best mate for thirty-five years. I’d have done anything for him. Anything.",
 "suspects:suspects.bryn.role": "The drummer",
 "suspects:suspects.carys.bio": "Rhys’s wife for seven years, and the person who runs his business: the deals, the diary, the social media. Before that she ran a PR firm in Cardiff. She has stayed on at Hafod this week, to be near where he died.",
 "suspects:suspects.carys.dismissal": "I don’t see what that has to do with my husband.",
 "suspects:suspects.carys.name": "Carys Morgan",
 "suspects:suspects.carys.rebuttal": "I’ve just lost my husband, and you want to tell me I did it? I was asleep in that house. Prove otherwise or leave me alone.",
 "suspects:suspects.carys.role": "The wife",
 "suspects:suspects.dean.bio": "Halflight’s guitarist, until he walked out in 1998. He wrote the music of ‘Small Hours’, he says, and never got the credit. These days he teaches guitar above a shop in Newport. He has been arrested for Rhys’s murder and is out on bail, forbidden to go back to Hafod.",
 "suspects:suspects.dean.dismissal": "You’ve lost me, butt.",
 "suspects:suspects.dean.name": "Dean Pritchard",
 "suspects:suspects.dean.rebuttal": "I shoved him. I’ve shoved him a hundred times since we were fifteen. I never pushed him down any steps, and I never would.",
 "suspects:suspects.dean.role": "The guitarist",
 "suspects:suspects.eddie.bio": "Halflight’s manager since 1994, when he heard them in a Newport pub and signed them on a beer mat. He put the reunion together, and the documentary, and the tour. He has been looking after Carys all week.",
